From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EmmanueleC <ai.emmanuelecrifasi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:36:04 +0100
Subject: game-mode: an opt-in Game Mode form of the Mac app
 (DM_APP_GAME_MODE=1 when packing, DM_LAUNCH_EXEC)

Ported from Fasen24-AI/swordboiMacNative 045309a7 (EmmanueleC, MIT). An app packed with DM_APP_GAME_MODE=1
asks for Game Mode (LSSupportsGameMode, GCSupportsGameMode) and its launcher hands its process to the host, so
macOS's Game Mode and the foreground app's scheduling apply to the host. Off by default: nxnative found Game
Mode holds the GPU clock low (frame-rate.md), so it needs an A/B first. In that form the cloud save's last send
waits for the next start and Restart game / quick-save loads end the game; an app off the startup volume keeps
the child host (macOS privacy checks refuse an exec'ed process's opens there).
---
 dm/mac/launcher.c     | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 dm/mac/pack_app.py    |  3 +++
 docs/env_switches.tsv |  4 ++++
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/mac/launcher.c b/dm/mac/launcher.c
index df4f8a44f8baf9de6c7e55f6c16afcd751a901f4..9664f2357795c066124653df21f73057de61126f 100644
--- a/dm/mac/launcher.c
+++ b/dm/mac/launcher.c
@@ -357,6 +357,23 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     unlink(restart); setenv("DM_LAUNCHER_RESTART", restart, 1);
     char slotreq[PATH_MAX]; snprintf(slotreq, sizeof slotreq, "%s/slot-load-requested", sup);   // quick-save slots (nxforge/launcher_slots.inc)
     unlink(slotreq); setenv("DM_LAUNCHER_SLOT_LOAD", slotreq, 1);
+    // Game Mode build (Info.plist DMLaunchExec 1, pack_app.py with DM_APP_GAME_MODE=1; DM_LAUNCH_EXEC=0 / 1 in the environment or an env file overrides it): the host takes this
+    // process's place instead of running as its child. macOS gives Game Mode and the foreground application's scheduling to the process LaunchServices started, the bundle's own,
+    // and a child gets neither (the window, the GPU work and the frame deadline are all the host's). What the child form does after the host exits is lost: the cloud save's last
+    // send waits for the next start, the log has no exit line, and NXForge's Restart game and quick-save slot loads (the loop below) end the game instead of starting it again. Not for an app off the startup volume: macOS privacy checks refuse every open on a removable volume to a
+    // process that was exec'ed (the reason the host is otherwise a child, top of this file), so the host runs as a child there
+    char exec_s[8] = ""; const char *ex = getenv("DM_LAUNCH_EXEC");
+    if (!ex && info_string("DMLaunchExec", exec_s, sizeof exec_s)) ex = exec_s;
+    if (ex && !strcmp(ex, "1")) {
+        struct stat root_st, host_st;
+        if (!stat("/System/Volumes/Data", &root_st) && !stat(host, &host_st) && root_st.st_dev != host_st.st_dev)
+            fprintf(stderr, "launcher: DM_LAUNCH_EXEC asked, but the app is not on the startup volume: the host runs as a child\n");
+        else {
+            fprintf(stderr, "launcher: the host takes this process's place (DM_LAUNCH_EXEC: Game Mode and the app's scheduling are the host's)\n");
+            execve(host, host_argv, environ);
+            fprintf(stderr, "[RED] launcher: exec of %s failed (%s): the host runs as a child\n", host, strerror(errno));
+        }
+    }
     int status;
     for (;;) {
         int err = posix_spawn(&g_child, host, NULL, NULL, host_argv, environ);
diff --git a/dm/mac/pack_app.py b/dm/mac/pack_app.py
index 4f0210e7bf830a3c25388fde3b319360b0502d0d..fd4b927eff8dcd8eb7aa28078b9ac451c1181858 100755
--- a/dm/mac/pack_app.py
+++ b/dm/mac/pack_app.py
@@ -130,6 +130,9 @@ def info_plist(a, minos, icon):
          'NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription': 'Connect Switch 2 Joy-Con and Pro Controllers over Bluetooth.',
          'LSApplicationCategoryType': a.category or 'public.app-category.games', 'LSSupportsGameMode': False, 'DMTitleID': a.title_id.upper(), 'DMRomfsMarker': a.marker or '', 'DMLanguage': a.lang or 'en-US', 'DMSaveSyncChoice': 1}
     if icon: p['CFBundleIconFile'] = 'AppIcon'
+    # DM_APP_GAME_MODE=1 when packing: an app that asks for Game Mode and whose launcher hands its process to the host (launcher.c DM_LAUNCH_EXEC), for a Mac where Game Mode
+    # helps more than its GPU clock rule costs. The default stays off, for the reason above
+    if os.environ.get('DM_APP_GAME_MODE') == '1': p['LSSupportsGameMode'] = True; p['GCSupportsGameMode'] = True; p['DMLaunchExec'] = '1'
     if a.settings:
         listed = json.loads(Path(a.settings).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))['settings']
         p['DMSettings'] = settings_rules(listed)
diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 75bbfaf5adc9abe5a05000752677a6c92b8dfb6d..12a4d71fb6ca46069a710d6e6de1c083dc45904e 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ DM_ANISO	diagnostic	`0`, `2`, `4`, `8` or `16`: anisotropic filtering of at leas
 DM_AOC_DIR	path	Folder of add-on content: one numbered subfolder per DLC index holding that DLC's RomFS, reported by `aoc` and mounted read-only; the app, the Mac launcher and the NSP script set it when the build has DLC
 DM_AOC_OWNED	switch	`0` reports no add-on content even when `DM_AOC_DIR` has some, for runs without the DLC
 DM_APP_DM	path	Set by the iOS app of a game of several programs: the running program's `dm/p<N>` folder, where the settings screen finds its `launcher.json`
+DM_APP_GAME_MODE	switch	`1` when packing (`pack_app.py`): the app asks for Game Mode (`LSSupportsGameMode`, `GCSupportsGameMode`) and its launcher hands its process to the host (`DMLaunchExec` 1, see `DM_LAUNCH_EXEC`)
 DM_APP_VERSION	switch	Overrides the IPA's version in `build_ipa.sh`; by default it is the packed game's display version from its control data (the update's when one is packed)
 DM_AUDIO	switch	`1` plays audio through Core Audio, `0` uses the silent sink; real output is the default on iOS, the silent sink on the Mac (the Mac launcher sets `1`)
 DM_AUDIO_CAPTURE	test	`=<file>`: `tests/t_audio_live.c` records the output device's input (a loopback device such as BlackHole) there as 32-bit float samples, for `dm/tools/audio_channel_check.py`
@@ -124,6 +125,8 @@ DM_KEYS	switch	Scripted input: `<seconds or f<frame>>:<key>[+key][~hold or ~f<fr
 DM_LANG	player	Game language as a language code (default `en-US`; the iOS app sets the one the IPA was packed with)
 DM_LAUNCHER	switch	`0` skips the iOS settings screen or the Mac settings window and starts the game at once, with the saved choices (on the Mac also `--no-launcher`)
 DM_LAUNCHER_RESTART	diagnostic	Set by the Mac launcher (dm/mac/launcher.c): the file Quick settings › Restart game writes before quitting, so the launcher starts the game again
+DM_LAUNCHER_SLOT_LOAD	path	File the in-game sidebar writes a quick-save slot's folder into before a restart; the launcher swaps that slot in with the host stopped (`dm/mac/nxforge/launcher_slots.inc`)
+DM_LAUNCH_EXEC	switch	`1` makes the Mac app's launcher hand its process to the host instead of running it as a child, so macOS's Game Mode and the foreground app's scheduling apply to the host (default: the bundle's `DMLaunchExec`, which `DM_APP_GAME_MODE=1` sets when packing); `0` keeps the child. An app off the startup volume keeps the child
 DM_LAUNCH_PARAM	path	File whose bytes `oe::TryPopLaunchParameter` returns once; `oe::ExecuteProgram` sets it for the program it starts; a relaunch removes it
 DM_LINK_VTICK	switch	`0` keeps the system's display-link rate on 144 or 165 Hz Mac screens; by default the link counts only the refreshes nearest a steady 1/60 s clock
 DM_LOADHASH	diagnostic	`=1` logs an address-independent SHA-256 per module after loading
@@ -434,6 +437,7 @@ DM_SHARED_FONT	path	One font file served for every shared-font type except the N
 DM_SHARED_FONT_EXT	path	Font file served for shared-font type 5, the Nintendo extension with the button icons (default `$DM_FONT_DIR/nintendo_ext.ttf`, made by `make_shared_fonts.py`)
 DM_SHOW_FPS	player	`1` shows the frame-rate counter on the iPhone (frames put on screen per second, top left); at IPA build it sets `DMShowFPS` in `Info.plist`, which `Documents/env.txt` overrides
 DM_SIX_DELAY	switch	`=0` (the default), `=auto` or `=<ms>` (up to 40): `DM_IMU_DELAY`'s playout delay for the six-axis states (`GetSixAxisSensorStates`) instead of the IMU samples. None by default: a Switch 1 game reads the newest state each frame (aiming, steering), so a delay only adds latency. Also through `DM_CTL`'s `env`
+DM_SLOT_LOADED	player	Set by the launcher for the host after a slot load: the slot's folder, or `!` and why it was not loaded; the sidebar's toast says which
 DM_SLOWFRAME	diagnostic	`=1` writes the per-frame timing breakdown to the log only for dropped frames (kept in a ring of the last 16 frames, judged 8 frames late)
 DM_SPIN	switch	`0` makes the rewriter's spin gate return at once, so guest poll loops spin with no sleep; the gate stays (on by default)
 DM_SPIN_LIST	diagnostic	`=1` makes `patch_nso.py` print every guest poll loop it found and sends through a spin gate
